pain:
  narrative: Your utility manages 200+ substations and 2M+ customers across diverse terrain, balancing legacy coal and natural gas plants with unpredictable solar and wind resources. SCADA operators work with 15-minute refresh rates and manual intervention protocols designed for a world that no longer exists. When wind output drops suddenly, there's no automated response—grid instability cascades, voltage sags ripple across districts, and you're left scrambling to shed load and prevent rolling blackouts. Meanwhile, you're curtailing (paying to throw away) perfectly good renewable generation because your system can't balance it in real-time. Your engineers are burned out managing a system that wasn't built for this complexity.
